A class object gets instantiated given the following actions:

<a> new or new done reflectively viz.,  newInstance / Class.forName

<b> static field from that class gets assigned

<c> subclass of that class suffers <a> / <b> 

<d> ClassLoader.loadClass is explicitly called

Typically classloader class has findClass that converts .class file to Class object and loadClass that controls the order
in which findClass is invoked for parent/child classloaders.

The traditional Java classloader model is that of parent delegation meaning given a requitest to findClass you punt to your 
parents all the way upto the bootclass loader and if not found then instantiate on your own. Of course if the class is already
instantiated none of this need be done and it can be returned immediately.

ClassLoader#loadClass
	ClassLoader#findClass ( take in string return Class<T> )
		ClassLoader#defineClass ( take in string return byte[] )


